  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_036, a multimodal multiprofile model using scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, and concat fusion, with validation accuracy 0.715 and F1 0.687. RNA-only results show multiprofile and scvi representations are promising, while image-only models are much weaker, so the main remaining uncertainty is how the RNA and image features should be combined. config_037 tests weighted fusion while keeping all other design choices identical to config_036, directly isolating the effect of fusion. This is an efficient one-factor extension of the current best direction: it can either improve performance or confirm that concat is the better fusion choice without confounding the result with changes to encoder, profile setting, or aggregation."
}

